{"duration": 43.337, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A coal miner carried a small bird deep underground.", "start": 0.05, "end": 2.397}, {"beat": 0, "text": "The bird rode in a cage, breathing faster than any man.", "start": 2.477, "end": 5.153}, {"beat": 0, "text": "The miner trusted this tiny creature with his life.", "start": 5.233, "end": 7.537}, {"beat": 1, "text": "The mine air could hide carbon monoxide, a gas with no smell.", "start": 7.737, "end": 10.767}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Miners could not see it, smell it, or feel it.", "start": 10.847, "end": 13.006}, {"beat": 1, "text": "It killed without warning.", "start": 13.086, "end": 14.302}, {"beat": 1, "text": "One breath of enough gas could stop a man's heart.", "start": 14.382, "end": 16.494}, {"beat": 2, "text": "You see, it's like a smoke detector beeping before you see flames.", "start": 16.694, "end": 19.531}, {"beat": 3, "text": "Canaries breathe faster and have a higher metabolism than miners.", "start": 19.731, "end": 22.674}, {"beat": 3, "text": "Their small bodies absorbed the poison first.", "start": 22.754, "end": 24.822}, {"beat": 3, "text": "The bird would collapse while the miners still felt fine.", "start": 24.902, "end": 27.227}, {"beat": 3, "text": "That collapse gave miners time to escape.", "start": 27.307, "end": 29.163}, {"beat": 3, "text": "The bird's distress was the alarm.", "start": 29.243, "end": 30.822}, {"beat": 4, "text": "John Scott Haldane proposed this idea in 1895.", "start": 31.022, "end": 34.115}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Canaries were used in mines as early as 1896.", "start": 34.195, "end": 37.03}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Modern sensors have replaced the birds.", "start": 37.11, "end": 38.986}, {"beat": 4, "text": "But the phrase 'canary in a coal mine' still warns us of hidden danger.", "start": 39.066, "end": 42.437}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.119, "end": 0.144, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "coal", "start": 0.194, "end": 0.344, "line": 0, "bea